Bring the pinned MaxDiffusion commit up on transformers 5 / huggingface_hub 1.

MAXDIFFUSION_COMMIT (68e0696) predates the upstream fixes for both halves of
the transformers 5 upgrade, so the FLUX text encoder patch alone is not enough
to get the pinned tree running. Two independent breakages, both already fixed
on maxdiffusion main and mirrored here:

1. Top-level transformers Flax imports raise on v5, before the model is even
   constructed:
     * max_utils.py                     -> FlaxCLIPTextModel, FlaxCLIPTextPreTrainedModel
     * pipelines/pipeline_flax_utils.py -> FlaxPreTrainedModel
     * pipelines/wan/wan_pipeline.py    -> FlaxCLIPVisionModel, from the
       transformers.models.clip.modeling_flax_clip module v5 deletes outright
   The first two are on the FLUX import chain (flux_pipeline imports
   FlaxDiffusionPipeline from pipeline_flax_utils; the trainer imports
   max_utils); the third breaks WAN. The isinstance and issubclass call sites
   are guarded too, so a None class object never reaches them. WAN only uses
   FlaxCLIPVisionModel for image-to-video and already tolerates it failing to
   load, so leaving it None degrades to that existing path.

2. transformers 5 requires huggingface_hub >= 1, which removed the
   use_auth_token kwarg. Three call sites pass it straight to a hub API and
   raise TypeError when loading the FLUX VAE and transformer:
     * configuration_utils.py             -> hf_hub_download
     * models/modeling_flax_utils.py      -> hf_hub_download
     * pipelines/pipeline_flax_utils.py   -> snapshot_download
   Renamed to token=, matching upstream. The remaining use_auth_token kwargs in
   the tree are passed between maxdiffusion functions, which still accept them.

Drop this patch once MAXDIFFUSION_COMMIT moves past those upstream fixes.

